  1767                                  ; ------------------------------------------------------------
  1768                                  ; cmd_edit: opens the built-in editor on an existing file. Edits a copy of
  1769                                  ; the file's content in place (typed chars/Enter insert at the cursor,
  1770                                  ; Backspace/Delete remove around it, Left/Right/Home/End move it - all
  1771                                  ; newline-aware), ESC ends editing and asks whether to save (y) or
  1772                                  ; discard (n).
  1773                                  ;
  1774                                  ; Loop state (kept in registers across the whole edit session, same
  1775                                  ; convention as cur_dir-style code elsewhere - callees here are all
  1776                                  ; expected to preserve r12-r15):
  1777                                  ;   r15 = node id being edited
  1778                                  ;   r14 = content length (bytes used in fs_io_buf)
  1779                                  ;   r13 = cursor index into fs_io_buf (0..r14)
  1780                                  ;   r12 = "top row" - the 0-based row number (counting both embedded
  1781                                  ;         newlines and 80-col wraps from the start of the buffer) that
  1782                                  ;         .ce_render currently shows at the top of the scrollable body.
  1783                                  ;
  1784                                  ; Unlike read_line (which only ever holds one un-wrapped line, so it can
