  6068                                  ; acpi_shutdown: real ACPI power-off, the mechanism real hardware
  6069                                  ; actually needs (the hardcoded emulator ports above are debug
  6070                                  ; shortcuts that only exist in software, not on physical machines).
  6071                                  ;
  6072                                  ; Steps (see the ACPI spec / OSDev wiki "Shutdown" page for the
  6073                                  ; equivalent C version of this):
  6074                                  ;   1) find the RSDP by scanning the EBDA and 0xE0000-0xFFFFF for the
  6075                                  ;      "RSD PTR " signature
  6076                                  ;   2) walk the RSDT (or XSDT on ACPI 2.0+) to find the FADT ("FACP")
  6077                                  ;   3) from the FADT, get the DSDT pointer and the PM1a/PM1b control
  6078                                  ;      ports, and enable ACPI mode via SMI_CMD if it isn't already on
  6079                                  ;   4) scan the DSDT's AML bytecode for the "_S5_" package, which
  6080                                  ;      encodes the SLP_TYPa/SLP_TYPb sleep-state values for power-off
  6081                                  ;   5) write (SLP_TYP | SLP_EN) to the PM1 control port(s)
  6082                                  ;
  6083                                  ; If any step fails (table missing, signature doesn't check out, etc)
  6084                                  ; this just returns and the caller falls back to the legacy ports.
  6085                                  ; Requires boot.asm's identity map to cover wherever these tables land
  6086                                  ; in physical memory - see the 64MB mapping in pm_entry.
