  6793                                  ; ============================================================
  6794                                  ;  BACKGROUND PARTY SCHEDULER
  6795                                  ;  A background .run is a Party program stepped cooperatively: it
  6796                                  ;  executes on its OWN private stack (proc_bg_stack) with its OWN
  6797                                  ;  parked interpreter state (proc_bg_ctx), so a background script
  6798                                  ;  nested in while loops / function calls can be paused at any
  6799                                  ;  statement boundary and resumed later without losing its call
  6800                                  ;  stack. The shared interpreter globals are parked into/restored
  6801                                  ;  from the process's ctx area around every step, which is what lets
  6802                                  ;  a foreground 'party'/'run' (or another background process) safely
  6803                                  ;  reuse them in between.
  6804                                  ; ============================================================
  6805                                  
  6806                                  ; bg_step_proc: rax = slot. Restores the process's interpreter state,
  6807                                  ; redirects putchar at its output ring, then switches to its private
  6808                                  ; stack and resumes it (the first step lands in party_bg_bootstrap,
  6809                                  ; later steps in the interpreter's own yield-resume point). Control
  6810                                  ; returns to the scheduler - as if this call simply returned - either
  6811                                  ; when the process yields after BG_QUANTUM statements or when it ends.
  6812                                  ; Note this never returns via a normal `ret` (the process stack's saved
  6813                                  ; top word is the resume IP), so it must NOT push anything after saving
  6814                                  ; bg_shell_rsp. Clobbers rax, rbx, rcx, rdx, rsi, rdi, r8-r15.
  6815                                  bg_step_proc:
