 11497                                  ; pci_pm_wake: force the device at nic_pci_bus/dev/func out of D3 into D0
 11498                                  ; via its PCI Power Management capability, if it has one. On real hardware,
 11499                                  ; firmware quite often leaves an onboard NIC parked in D3hot at handoff
 11500                                  ; (or a previous OS's ACPI driver put it there and a warm reset didn't
 11501                                  ; clear it) - config/IO/MMIO reads and writes to a device in D3 are
 11502                                  ; unreliable (commonly read back as all-1s/garbage, writes silently
 11503                                  ; dropped), so every other fix in the bring-up path is moot until this
 11504                                  ; runs. QEMU's virtual devices are always already in D0, which is why
 11505                                  ; this was invisible there. Walks the capabilities list from offset 0x34
 11506                                  ; looking for PCI_CAP_ID_PM (0x01), clears the PowerState bits in PMCSR
 11507                                  ; (cap_ptr+4) to select D0, then waits >=10ms per the PCI PM spec before
 11508                                  ; the device's config space is touched again. No-op if the device has no
 11509                                  ; PM capability, or is already in D0.
