 12656                                      ; Wait for the chip to clear OWN on this slot. QEMU clears it almost
 12657                                      ; immediately, so a raw loop count worked there; on real hardware the
 12658                                      ; first TX DMA after link bring-up can take far longer than a cached-
 12659                                      ; RAM spin allows (the loop reads the descriptor from the CPU cache,
 12660                                      ; which outruns the NIC's write-back by orders of magnitude). So wait
 12661                                      ; on wall-clock RTC seconds instead: up to ~2s, re-kicking TPPoll each
 12662                                      ; second in case the chip needed another poll to notice the slot.
 12663                                      ; NOTE: budget is in whole-second ticks, but the tick boundary itself
 12664                                      ; consumes no polling time - see the js/jz fix below. With r11d=N we
 12665                                      ; get the remainder of the current second plus N full subsequent
 12666                                      ; seconds of continuous OWN polling before giving up. Bumped from 2 to
 12667                                      ; 5: field reports on real hardware still showed OWN clearing (and
 12668                                      ; NPQ already down) moments after a "failure" even with the earlier
 12669                                      ; 2-3s budget, especially around ring wraparound (EOR slot) - so the
 12670                                      ; occasional real-world completion is simply slower than that.
