 12675                                                                    ; so netdiag_dump_tx can report real elapsed
 12676                                                                    ; wall-clock time on failure, not just a tick
 12677                                                                    ; count that's always the same constant.
 12678                                      ; Bumped 5 -> 20: with rtc_sec_now's BCD bug fixed we can finally trust
 12679                                      ; the elapsed-time diagnostic, but the last two runs still failed with
 12680                                      ; an identical signature (no PCI error, NPQ/OWN both eventually clear)
 12681                                      ; even after padding ruled out short-frame handling as the cause. That
 12682                                      ; points at this chip/link genuinely needing longer than 5-6s for its
 12683                                      ; first TX after an idle gap (e.g. PHY/EEE low-power wake, or link
 12684                                      ; re-training) rather than a logic bug in the wait itself. Widening
 12685                                      ; the budget is a cheap way to confirm that: if this send now
