 14116                                  ; dns_query: rsi = hostname (null-terminated). If it's already a dotted
 14117                                  ; quad, returns eax = IP. Otherwise sends a DNS A query to nic_dns:53,
 14118                                  ; waits for the reply, and returns eax = IP, or 0xFFFFFFFF on failure.
 14119                                  ;
 14120                                  ; DNS_ROUND_SECS / DNS_MAX_RETRIES: the wait budget used to be a single
 14121                                  ; ~1-second tick plus one immediate resend, then an outright fail on the
 14122                                  ; very next tick -- worst case barely over a second, best case under two.
 14123                                  ; That's nowhere near enough for a real round trip through QEMU's
 14124                                  ; user-mode DNS proxy (which itself has to go ask a real resolver), so
 14125                                  ; a perfectly healthy query could -- and did -- report "could not
 14126                                  ; resolve host" moments after its reply had actually left the wire (see
 14127                                  ; the trace: the "rx ... sport=0x0035" DNS reply prints, immediately
 14128                                  ; followed by "could not resolve host"). Mirror the same fix already
 14129                                  ; applied to tcp_send_segment's wait loop and nic_arp_resolve: a
 14130                                  ; multi-second budget per round, several resend rounds before giving up.
 14131                                  DNS_ROUND_SECS equ 5
 14132                                  DNS_MAX_RETRIES equ 3
