   526                              <1> ; ============================================================
   527                              <1> ;  MODULES  (Phase 5)
   528                              <1> ; ============================================================
   529                              <1> ; A line of the form
   530                              <1> ;     module "otherfile.pa"
   531                              <1> ; splices that file's whole text in at that point, before lexing -
   532                              <1> ; a textual include, same idea as C's #include or Python's exec of
   533                              <1> ; another file's source. This is the simplest way to add
   534                              <1> ; multi-file scripts without teaching the rest of the interpreter
   535                              <1> ; (one token array over one source buffer - see party_lex's header
   536                              <1> ; comment) about which file a token or a function body came from:
   537                              <1> ; flatten everything into one buffer first, then lex/collect/run
   538                              <1> ; exactly as before. A module is typically just function
   539                              <1> ; definitions meant to be called from the including script, but
   540                              <1> ; nothing stops it from having top-level statements too - those run
   541                              <1> ; in place, in file order, same as if they'd been pasted in by hand.
   542                              <1> ;
   543                              <1> ; Include cycles and repeats are handled the boring way: each
   544                              <1> ; resolved path is only ever expanded once per party_expand_modules
   545                              <1> ; call (party_module_names), and nesting depth is capped
   546                              <1> ; (PARTY_MODULE_DEPTH_MAX) so a module that (perhaps indirectly)
   547                              <1> ; includes itself fails cleanly instead of recursing forever.
   548                              <1> ; ------------------------------------------------------------
   549                              <1> 
   550                              <1> PARTY_MODULE_MAX       equ 8    ; distinct module files one script may include
   551                              <1> PARTY_MODULE_DEPTH_MAX equ 3    ; how deeply modules may include modules
   552                              <1> PARTY_MOD_PATH_MAX     equ 200  ; NUL-terminated module-path staging size
   553                              <1> 
   554                              <1> ; party_expand_modules: expands `module "..."` lines in fs_io_buf in
   555                              <1> ; place (fs_io_buf holds the just-read main script on entry).
   556                              <1> ; Out: party_preproc_ok = 1 on success, fs_io_buf now holds the fully
   557                              <1> ; expanded source. On failure, party_preproc_ok = 0,
   558                              <1> ; party_preproc_err_ptr names the problem (and, for a not-found
   559                              <1> ; module, party_preproc_bad_path holds the offending path) - fs_io_buf
   560                              <1> ; is left untouched. Clobbers rax-rdx, rsi, rdi, r8-r15.
