  1556                              <1> ; ------------------------------------------------------------
  1557                              <1> ;  BACKGROUND PROCESS CONTEXT SAVE / RESTORE
  1558                              <1> ;  party_ctx_save(rdi = dst ctx base) parks the whole mutable
  1559                              <1> ;  interpreter state (token stream, value stack, variable/locals/
  1560                              <1> ;  function/call-frame tables, all scalars, the live statement cursor)
  1561                              <1> ;  into a process's proc_bg_ctx area. party_ctx_restore(rsi = src ctx
  1562                              <1> ;  base) brings it all back before a background step resumes. The
  1563                              <1> ;  regions copied are listed in party_ctx_table (src-address/size
  1564                              <1> ;  pairs, zero-terminated); r13 (statement cursor), r14 (stop token)
  1565                              <1> ;  and r15 (branch flag) are parked after the data block. Used both by
  1566                              <1> ;  cmd_run_back (parks the freshly lexed+collected state before the
  1567                              <1> ;  first step) and party_bg_suspend (parks a mid-run state at a yield).
  1568                              <1> ;  Both clobber rax, rbx, rcx, rsi, rdi, r8-r15.
  1569                              <1> ; ------------------------------------------------------------
  1570                              <1> ; PARTY_CTX_SIZE was 20226 through Phase 3. Phase 4 adds 32 bytes
  1571                              <1> ; (party_scratch3, folded into the existing party_scratch region
  1572                              <1> ; below) + 2084 bytes (the new party_arr_used/count/data regions:
  1573                              <1> ; PARTY_ARR_MAX + PARTY_ARR_MAX*8 + PARTY_ARR_MAX*PARTY_ARR_CAP*32 =
  1574                              <1> ; 4 + 32 + 2048), so 20226 + 32 + 2084 = 22342. Bumping
  1575                              <1> ; PARTY_MAX_TOKENS from 512 to 2048 grows the token-array entry below
  1576                              <1> ; from 4098 (2 + 512*8) to 16386 (2 + 2048*8), a delta of 12288, so
  1577                              <1> ; 22342 + 12288 = 34630. Bumping PARTY_ARR_CAP from 16 to 80 grows
  1578                              <1> ; party_arr_data from 2048 to 10240 (4*80*32), a delta of 8192, so
  1579                              <1> ; 34630 + 8192 = 42822. This constant is NOT auto-derived from
  1580                              <1> ; party_ctx_table below - if that table's per-entry sizes change
  1581                              <1> ; again, update this by hand to match, the same way this session had
  1582                              <1> ; to (three times now).
  1583                              <1> PARTY_CTX_REGS_OFFS equ 42822 - 24
  1584                              <1> PARTY_CTX_SIZE      equ 42822
  1585                              <1> 
