  5118                              <1> ;  SCREEN + TIMING BUILTINS  (Phase 6)
  5119                              <1> ; ============================================================
  5120                              <1> ; sleep/gotoxy are the two primitives §13's "true matrix rain needs
  5121                              <1> ; independent columns" note was waiting on: sleep(ms) throttles a
  5122                              <1> ; frame loop instead of busy-spinning it at full CPU speed, and
  5123                              <1> ; gotoxy(x,y) repositions the cursor so a script can address any
  5124                              <1> ; screen cell directly instead of only ever appending at the bottom.
  5125                              <1> ; Both route straight to kernel.asm primitives (sleep_ms,
  5126                              <1> ; kernel_gotoxy) - see the TIMING/SLEEP and CURSOR ADDRESSING
  5127                              <1> ; sections there for how the delay is actually measured (RDTSC,
  5128                              <1> ; calibrated once at boot - there's no PIT/IRQ0 timer) and why
  5129                              <1> ; gotoxy doesn't scroll or draw anything itself.
  5130                              <1> 
  5131                              <1> ; ---- sleep(ms) -> none; busy-waits ms milliseconds. Esc still
  5132                              <1> ; aborts a long sleep early (sleep_ms polls kill_flag itself), same
  5133                              <1> ; as any other statement - see party_exec_stmts's kill check. ----
