   711                              <1> .sendfail:
   712                              <1>     ; nic_arp_resolve records WHY the send failed: a genuine raw-TX/hardware
   713                              <1>     ; problem (reason 0) versus the broadcast going out fine but nobody ever
   714                              <1>     ; answering it (reason 1). These are very different situations and used
   715                              <1>     ; to be reported identically as a "TX error - link/chip problem", which
   716                              <1>     ; is actively misleading when the NIC itself did nothing wrong.
