   724                              <1>     ; this distinguishes a bus-level error (abort/parity) from the descriptor
   725                              <1>     ; engine silently never touching the slot. Only meaningful for a genuine
   726                              <1>     ; raw-TX failure, so skip it entirely for the no-reply case above.
   727 0003774E 803C25[44CA0800]02  <1>     cmp byte [nic_driver_type], 2
