     1                              <1> ; ============================================================
     2                              <1> ;  crypto.asm -- SHA-256 / HMAC-SHA256 / HKDF (Phase 1 of the
     3                              <1> ;  https.asm build plan -- see phases.txt)
     4                              <1> ;
     5                              <1> ;  This file is freestanding: no syscalls, no libc, nothing beyond
     6                              <1> ;  the register-save-everything-it-touches convention used across
     7                              <1> ;  the rest of the kernel (tcp.asm / http.asm). It is intentionally
     8                              <1> ;  identical in algorithmic content to the crypto_core.inc.asm that
     9                              <1> ;  was verified standalone under Linux against RFC/NIST test
    10                              <1> ;  vectors before being ported here -- only the self-test command
    11                              <1> ;  at the bottom (cryptotest) is kernel-specific, using
    12                              <1> ;  print_string / print_hex8 instead of write(2).
    13                              <1> ;
    14                              <1> ;  Verified against reference vectors (see cmd_cryptotest below):
    15                              <1> ;    - SHA-256("") / SHA-256("abc") / NIST 1,000,000x'a' vector /
    16                              <1> ;      a split multi-call sha256_update (incremental buffering path)
    17                              <1> ;    - HMAC-SHA256 RFC 4231 test cases 1, 2, 6 (case 6 exercises the
    18                              <1> ;      "key longer than one block gets hashed down" path)
