  1448                              <1> ;  ChaCha20 block function + stream encrypt (RFC 8439 section 2.3/2.4)
  1449                              <1> ;  Ported from chacha20.asm (standalone scratch, verified against RFC
  1450                              <1> ;  8439 2.3.2/2.4.2 test vectors -- see phases.txt Phase 2). The
  1451                              <1> ;  scratch version didn't yet follow this kernel's "callee saves
  1452                              <1> ;  everything it touches" convention (it only saved the registers it
  1453                              <1> ;  used as explicit scratch across the QR macro's own sub-calls, not
  1454                              <1> ;  every register the caller might have live); both entry points below
  1455                              <1> ;  now save/restore every general-purpose register they touch, per
  1456                              <1> ;  the convention already used by sha256_hash/hmac_sha256 in this file.
  1457                              <1> ; ============================================================
