  1937                              <1> ; ============================================================
  1938                              <1> ;  ChaCha20-Poly1305 AEAD (RFC 8439 section 2.8)
  1939                              <1> ;  Ported from aead.asm (standalone scratch, verified against RFC 8439
  1940                              <1> ;  2.8.2 "Sunscreen" -- the vector with AAD -- plus decrypt round-trip
  1941                              <1> ;  and tampered-tag rejection; see phases.txt Phase 2). Differences
  1942                              <1> ;  from the scratch version: no `section .data` (kernel.asm has no
  1943                              <1> ;  sections -- these globals just follow the code, same as everything
  1944                              <1> ;  else in this file), and aead_memcpy/aead_zero_advance/aead_mem_eq
  1945                              <1> ;  (small internal helpers, same register-passed pattern as
  1946                              <1> ;  poly1305's sub-helpers) now document their clobber lists instead
  1947                              <1> ;  of silently clobbering; the two public entry points save/restore
  1948                              <1> ;  everything they touch.
  1949                              <1> ;
  1950                              <1> ;  All working state (key/nonce/buffer pointers, the one-time Poly1305
  1951                              <1> ;  key, and the assembled MAC-input buffer) lives in static globals
  1952                              <1> ;  rather than being threaded through registers/stack across the
  1953                              <1> ;  several sub-calls this needs -- matches the kernel's single-
  1954                              <1> ;  threaded, no-heap, no-recursion style. NOT reentrant; fine for a
  1955                              <1> ;  polled kernel with no concurrency.
  1956                              <1> ;
  1957                              <1> ;  chacha20_poly1305_encrypt(rdi=ct_out, rsi=tag_out16, rdx=pt,
  1958                              <1> ;    rcx=pt_len, r8=aad, r9=aad_len, [rsp+8]=key32, [rsp+16]=nonce12)
  1959                              <1> ;    Caller convention for the two stack args: `push nonce` then
  1960                              <1> ;    `push key` then `call`. The CALLEE pops them (via `ret 16`) --
  1961                              <1> ;    caller does NOT `add rsp,16` itself; for _decrypt that `add`
  1962                              <1> ;    would clobber CF before it could be tested with jc/jnc. Popping
  1963                              <1> ;    via `ret 16` clears the args as part of the return itself,
  1964                              <1> ;    without touching flags, so CF survives intact.
  1965                              <1> ;    Encrypts pt->ct_out and writes the 16-byte tag to tag_out16.
  1966                              <1> ;
  1967                              <1> ;  chacha20_poly1305_decrypt(rdi=pt_out, rsi=ct, rdx=ct_len, rcx=aad,
  1968                              <1> ;    r8=aad_len, r9=tag16, [rsp+8]=key32, [rsp+16]=nonce12) -> CF
  1969                              <1> ;    Same stack-arg convention. Verifies tag16 against a freshly
  1970                              <1> ;    computed tag over (aad,ct) BEFORE decrypting. CF=1 (pt_out left
  1971                              <1> ;    untouched) on tag mismatch; CF=0 and pt_out holds the decrypted
  1972                              <1> ;    plaintext on success. Correct call site:
  1973                              <1> ;        push nonce
  1974                              <1> ;        push key
  1975                              <1> ;        call chacha20_poly1305_decrypt
  1976                              <1> ;        jc .auth_fail        ; no add rsp,16 -- ret 16 already did it
  1977                              <1> ; ============================================================
  1978                              <1> 
  1979                              <1> ; Sized for the real worst case, not an arbitrary round number: this
  1980                              <1> ; buffer holds aad || pad16(aad) || ct || pad16(ct) || 16 bytes of
  1981                              <1> ; length trailer, and aead_build_mac_data below copies into it using
  1982                              <1> ; whatever aead_ct_len the caller set -- with no bounds check. For
  1983                              <1> ; chacha20_poly1305_decrypt that length is a TLS record's ciphertext
  1984                              <1> ; length straight off the wire, and TLS records go up to 16384 bytes
  1985                              <1> ; (tls.asm's TLS_RX_BUF_SIZE) - a single encrypted handshake flight
  1986                              <1> ; (EncryptedExtensions+Certificate+CertificateVerify+Finished) from a
  1987                              <1> ; real server routinely exceeds the old 4096-byte budget here, which
  1988                              <1> ; silently overran this buffer into whatever data follows it in the
  1989                              <1> ; flat kernel image. 16384 (max ct) + 16 (aad padded to 16) + 15 (ct's
  1990                              <1> ; own padding, up to 15 extra bytes) + 16 (length trailer) = 16431
  1991                              <1> ; worst case; rounded up with headroom.
  1992                              <1> AEAD_MAC_SCRATCH_SIZE equ 16640
  1993                              <1> 
  1994                              <1> ; ---- aead_align16: rax = align_up(rax, 16). Clobbers nothing else. ----
  1995                              <1> aead_align16:
  1996 00039BDC 4883C00F            <1>     add rax, 15
  1997 00039BE0 4883E0F0            <1>     and rax, ~15
  1998 00039BE4 C3                  <1>     ret
  1999                              <1> 
  2000                              <1> ; ---- aead_build_mac_data: builds the RFC 8439 2.8 MAC input into
  2001                              <1> ; aead_mac_scratch: aad || pad16(aad) || ct || pad16(ct) ||
  2002                              <1> ; len(aad) LE64 || len(ct) LE64. Reads aead_aad_ptr/aead_aad_len/
  2003                              <1> ; aead_ct_ptr/aead_ct_len (globals). Returns the total length in rax.
  2004                              <1> ; Clobbers rax,rbx,rcx,rdx,rsi,rdi (internal helper, register-passed
  2005                              <1> ; like poly1305's sub-helpers; both callers below save around it). ----
