   542                              <1>     ; ---- patch server_name ext length ----
   543                              <1>     ; server_name ext starts at r13 (its id), data begins r13+4.
   544                              <1>     ; ext data len = rdi - (r13+4) - (data len fields...) = rdi - r13 - 4
   545                              <1>     ; but we already wrote the "data length" field as 3+hostlen before
   546                              <1>     ; the name type. The overall ext length field (the one after the
   547                              <1>     ; 2-byte id) is data_len + 2 (vector u16) ... The tls_ref encoding:
   548                              <1>     ;   u16(0x0000) + u16(5+hostlen) + u16(3+hostlen) + u8(0) + u16(hostlen) + hostname
   549                              <1>     ; The "5+hostlen" is ext_data_len = (3+hostlen) + 2. And "3+hostlen"
   550                              <1>     ; is server_name_list length = u8(0)+u16(hostlen)+hostname = 3+hostlen.
   551                              <1>     ; We wrote u16(3+hostlen) as the list length field correctly, and
   552                              <1>     ; u16(5+hostlen) as ext data len. That matches tls_ref.
   553                              <1>     ; No patch needed: values were written correctly above.
