  2242                              <1> ; ============================================================
  2243                              <1> ;  tls_do_exchange -- Phase 4. Mirrors http.asm's tcp_do_exchange
  2244                              <1> ;  contract, but TLS-wrapped end to end: TCP connect -> TLS handshake
  2245                              <1> ;  (Phase 3) -> encrypt+send the request -> receive/decrypt the reply
  2246                              <1> ;  (looping over possibly multiple TCP segments/TLS records, same
  2247                              <1> ;  "no new data for a full tick means done" coalescing tcp_do_exchange
  2248                              <1> ;  uses -- here that patience comes from tls_wait_for_record's own
  2249                              <1> ;  TCP_ROUND_SECS/TCP_MAX_RETRIES budget, so there's still only ONE
  2250                              <1> ;  timeout scheme in the whole client, not a second one bolted on) ->
  2251                              <1> ;  send close_notify -> TCP FIN.
  2252                              <1> ;
  2253                              <1> ;  IN:  rsi = hostname (null-terminated), dx = port.
  2254                              <1> ;       Caller has already placed the plaintext request in
  2255                              <1> ;       tls_app_tx_buf with its length in tls_app_tx_len. (Buffer
  2256                              <1> ;       sizing decision, per phases.txt Phase 4 point 4: tls_app_tx_buf
  2257                              <1> ;       / tls_app_rx_buf are dedicated buffers, sized off http.asm's
  2258                              <1> ;       HTTP_TX_MAX=1200 / HTTP_RX_BUF_SIZE=3072 with headroom --
  2259                              <1> ;       TLS_APP_TX_MAX=2048, TLS_APP_RX_MAX=4096 -- rather than reusing
  2260                              <1> ;       tcp_tx_buf/tcp_rx_buf directly. tcp_tx_buf/tcp_rx_buf stay
  2261                              <1> ;       exactly as they are for the plain-HTTP path (cmd_tcp / a future
  2262                              <1> ;       plain take/give), so this Phase cannot regress them. The
  2263                              <1> ;       already-existing tls_tx_buf (sized TLS_RX_BUF_SIZE+64) is reused
