  1386                              <1> ; ============================================================
  1387                              <1> ;  mksin: build a .sin package from a prepared folder
  1388                              <1> ; ============================================================
  1389                              <1> ; `mksin <folder>` packages an already-prepared folder (one
  1390                              <1> ; containing "whattodo.inst" as a file and "files" as a folder,
  1391                              <1> ; exactly the layout spec section 10/11 requires inside a .sin)
  1392                              <1> ; into "<folder>.sin", ready for `install`.
  1393                              <1> ;
  1394                              <1> ; This does NOT reimplement zip writing: it validates the folder's
  1395                              <1> ; structure and whattodo.inst script first (catching an unknown
  1396                              <1> ; instruction, a missing argument, or a "copy" source that doesn't
  1397                              <1> ; actually exist under files/ - all *before* anything is written),
  1398                              <1> ; then hands off to the existing `pack` command (see zip.asm) to do
  1399                              <1> ; the real stored-mode zipping into "<folder>.zip", and finally
  1400                              <1> ; renames that node to "<folder>.sin" in place - the same in-place
  1401                              <1> ; node_name edit cmd_rname already uses, so no new archive-writing
  1402                              <1> ; code is needed at all.
  1403                              <1> ;
  1404                              <1> ; Known gaps:
  1405                              <1> ;   - Validation only checks the shape of whattodo.inst (known
  1406                              <1> ;     instructions, required args, absolute-looking destinations,
  1407                              <1> ;     and that "copy" sources exist under files/). It can't catch
  1408                              <1> ;     everything `install` might still reject (e.g. a destination
  1409                              <1> ;     that collides with a same-named FOLDER on the *target*
  1410                              <1> ;     machine) since that depends on where it's eventually
  1411                              <1> ;     installed, not on anything visible here.
  1412                              <1> ;   - Leans on `pack`'s own limits (EDIT_MAX total size, 64 files)
  1413                              <1> ;     and its own "refuses if <folder>.zip already exists" rule -
  1414                              <1> ;     mksin checks for a colliding <folder>.zip up front so that
  1415                              <1> ;     failure is reported as an mksin error instead of a raw pack
  1416                              <1> ;     one, but the actual cap enforcement still happens inside pack.
  1417                              <1> ; ------------------------------------------------------------
