 18991                                  
 18992                                  ; extra headers appended by both http_build_get and http_build_post, right
 18993                                  ; after Host: and before the blank line that ends the header block. A
 18994                                  ; request with no User-Agent/Accept at all is unusual enough that some
 18995                                  ; CDN/WAF edges (Fastly, the infra fronting GitHub Pages included) just
 18996                                  ; drop it -- closing the TLS session cleanly (handshake OK, close_notify,
 18997                                  ; zero HTTP bytes back) instead of returning any actual HTTP response.
 18998                                  ; That looked exactly like "stake: no body in response." even though
 18999                                  ; nothing in the TLS/record layer was at fault.
 19000 000A187A 557365722D4167656E-     http_extra_headers: db "User-Agent: rush/1.0", 13, 10, "Accept: */*", 13, 10, "Connection: close", 13, 10, 0
